NAME
    man - display a command's manual page

SYNOPSIS
    man [command]

DESCRIPTION
    Looks up and prints the manual page for <command> (case-insensitive)
    from the shell's dianash/man directory. If no detailed manual page
    exists for a registered command, prints its one-line usage entry.

    With no argument, man prints the full command summary produced by
    help(1).

EXAMPLES
    man
    man watch
    man hier

EXIT STATUS
    0   Manual page or usage printed.
    1   No manual entry or command exists for <command>.

SEE ALSO
    help(1), which(1), hier(7)
